---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO_URL, UPSTREAM_URL } from "../lib/releases";
---

<Base
  title="Source — SparkyBin Browser"
  description="Build SparkyBin Browser from source. Meson, a flatpak manifest, and a container recipe that needs nothing installed on the host."
>
  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-16 pb-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">Source</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">Build it yourself</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-soft">
        The whole thing is on GitHub, under the GNU GPL v3. Clone it, install a
        few libraries, and it builds.
      </p>
      <a
        href={REPO_URL}
        class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-bg transition-transform hover:-translate-y-px"
      >
        Open the repository <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">With meson</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
          The build needs WebKitGTK 6, GTK 4, libadwaita, json-glib, libsoup 3
          and a few more. The
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/HACKING.md`}>HACKING.md</a>
          file in the repository has the full list, and a container recipe that
          installs nothing on the host.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-rule bg-surface">
          <div class="border-b border-rule px-4 py-2.5">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint">sh</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[0.8rem] leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> git clone https://github.com/camroybal/SparkyBin-Browser.git
<span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> cd SparkyBin-Browser
<span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> meson setup build
<span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> ninja -C build
<span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> build/src/sparkybin-browser</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-semibold">With flatpak</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
          There are three manifests, one for each channel. The stable one is
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">com.sparkybin.Browser.json</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-rule bg-surface">
          <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[0.8rem] leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-ink-soft">$</span> flatpak-builder --user --install build \
      com.sparkybin.Browser.json</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Contributing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
          Patches are welcome. The project follows the GNOME conventions for
          commit messages, and the
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a>
          file says what to put in a bug report and which problems belong to
          WebKit rather than to the browser.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-semibold">Reporting a problem</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>The issue tracker</a>
          is on GitHub. Problems with how a page renders, with JavaScript or
          with video playback belong to
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="https://bugs.webkit.org/">WebKit Bugzilla</a>
          instead, and the guide says which is which.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-semibold">The upstream</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
          This is a fork of
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={UPSTREAM_URL}>GNOME Web</a>,
          last synced with the 51.1 release. The changes made to it are
          recorded in the
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/NOTICE`}>NOTICE</a>
          file, and the original copyright notices are kept.
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-rule bg-bg-tint px-4 py-3 text-sm text-ink-soft"
        >
          SparkyBin Browser is not affiliated with, authorized by, sponsored by
          or endorsed by the GNOME Foundation.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
